            coordinates { (0,0) (60,0) };
        \end{axis}
        \end{tikzpicture}
      </latex-image>
    </image>
  </figure>
  <p>
    This residual plot looks pretty good. The residuals are balanced
    above and below the line, they are relatively small residuals, and
    there is no obvious pattern. This is evidence of a good linear
    regression: a line that fits the data well.
  </p>
  <p>
    <xref ref="figure-linear-model3"/> is another scatter plot with
    <xref ref="figure-residual-plot3"/> as it residual plot. 
  </p>
  <figure xml:id="figure-linear-model3">
    <caption>Another linear model</caption>
    <image xml:id="image-linear-model3" width="80%">
      <latex-image>
        \begin{tikzpicture}
          \begin{axis}[
            xlabel={x},
            ylabel={y},
            ]
